{
  "uid": "pg-monitoring",
  "title": "PostgreSQL: Monitoring Health",
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "refresh": "5m",
  "time": {
    "from": "now-6h",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "annotations": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "Failover",
        "enable": true,
        "iconColor": "red",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "expr": "changes(pg_timeline_id[2m]) > 0",
        "step": "60s",
        "target": {
          "expr": "changes(pg_timeline_id[2m]) > 0",
          "refId": "Anno"
        },
        "titleFormat": "Promote / failover",
        "textFormat": "{{node}}: timeline changed (promote)"
      },
      {
        "name": "PostgreSQL restart",
        "enable": true,
        "iconColor": "orange",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "expr": "resets(pg_postmaster_uptime_seconds[5m]) > 0",
        "step": "60s",
        "target": {
          "expr": "resets(pg_postmaster_uptime_seconds[5m]) > 0",
          "refId": "Anno"
        },
        "titleFormat": "PostgreSQL restart",
        "textFormat": "{{node}}"
      },
      {
        "name": "Stats reset",
        "enable": true,
        "iconColor": "blue",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "expr": "resets(pg_statements_calls_total[10m]) > 0",
        "step": "60s",
        "target": {
          "expr": "resets(pg_statements_calls_total[10m]) > 0",
          "refId": "Anno"
        },
        "titleFormat": "pg_stat_statements reset",
        "textFormat": "{{node}} — counters restarted from zero"
      }
    ]
  },
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "node",
        "label": "Нода",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(pg_up, node)",
          "refId": "var"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "current": {
          "text": "pg01",
          "value": "pg01"
        },
        "description": "Идентичность НОДЫ, не роль: после failover нода остаётся собой. Роль показывают панели Node Roles / pg_role_info."
      },
      {
        "name": "host",
        "label": "Хост",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "prometheus"
        },
        "query": {
          "query": "label_values(pg_up{node=~\"$node\"}, host)",
          "refId": "var"
        },
        "refresh": 2,
        "sort": 1,
        "includeAll": false,
        "multi": false,
        "current": {
          "text": "demo-host",
          "value": "demo-host"
        }
      }
    ]
  },
  "links": [
    {
      "title": "← Overview",
      "type": "link",
      "icon": "dashboard",
      "url": "/d/pg-overview",
      "keepTime": true,
      "includeVars": true,
      "asDropdown": false,
      "targetBlank": false,
      "tags": []
    }
  ],
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 701,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Scrape Targets",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "up{host=~\"$host\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{job}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "up{job=\"prometheus\"}",
          "legendFormat": "prometheus",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "description": "OK: all = 1. Fix: whichever job is down — that monitoring layer is blind; absent() alerts must catch this."
    },
    {
      "id": 702,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Scrape Duration",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "scrape_duration_seconds{host=~\"$host\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{job}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "OK: well below the 10s timeout. Fix: close to 10s — a heavy collector; see rollback triggers in rollback_cumulative_stats.txt."
    },
    {
      "id": 703,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Scrape Samples vs Limit",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 0
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "scrape_samples_post_metric_relabeling{job=~\"sql-.*\",host=~\"$host\"}",
          "legendFormat": "{{job}}",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "vector(8000)",
          "legendFormat": "sample_limit (prometheus.yml)",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Watch: approaching sample_limit — exceeding it drops the WHOLE scrape. Fix: cardinality (top-N, labels) or raise the limit in prometheus.yml (the 8000 line is hardcoded)."
    },
    {
      "id": 704,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "pgss Evictions",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "increase(pg_statements_dealloc_total{host=~\"$host\"}[1h])",
          "legendFormat": "{{job}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Watch: dealloc growth = top-N silently undercounts. Fix: raise pg_stat_statements.max or reset more often."
    },
    {
      "id": 705,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "TSDB Head Series",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "prometheus_tsdb_head_series",
          "legendFormat": "head series",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "description": "Watch: growth steps = cardinality explosion. Fix: find the culprit via count by (__name__), sample_limit guards."
    },
    {
      "id": 706,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "PostgreSQL Reachability (pg_up)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 16,
        "y": 7
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "noValue": "no data — exporter down",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "pg_up",
          "legendFormat": "{{node}}",
          "refId": "A",
          "instant": true
        },
        {
          "expr": "pg_database_up",
          "legendFormat": "{{node}} {{datname}}",
          "refId": "B",
          "instant": true
        }
      ],
      "description": "The OTHER half of Scrape Targets: up covers Prometheus→exporter, pg_up covers exporter→PostgreSQL (expired password, moved DSN, network), and pg_database_up covers the per-database DSNs of the object collectors (pgNN-appdb jobs) — without it a dropped appdb or revoked grant is only visible as object metrics silently vanishing. up=1 with pg_up=0 = the exporter is alive but the database is unreachable. When the exporter itself dies the series disappear — that renders as «no data» here and up=0 in Scrape Targets."
    },
    {
      "id": 707,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Dropped Scrapes (limits hit)",
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "prometheus"
      },
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 7,
        "w": 8,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 14
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short",
          "min": 0
        },
        "overrides": []
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(prometheus_target_scrapes_exceeded_sample_limit_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "sample_limit exceeded (scrape dropped)",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "sum(increase(prometheus_target_scrape_pool_exceeded_label_limits_total[$__rate_interval]))",
          "legendFormat": "label_limits exceeded (pool sync)",
          "refId": "B"
        }
      ],
      "description": "The FACT of a dropped scrape, not the approach to it (that is Scrape Samples vs Limit): every point here = a whole scrape thrown away, a hole in every metric of that node. OK: flat zero. Fix: cut cardinality (top-N, labels) or raise sample_limit/label_limit in prometheus.yml. A per-scrape label_limit violation has no dedicated counter — it fails the scrape and shows as up=0 in Scrape Targets."
    }
  ]
}
